1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,300
Captain Kim Junho sat with the phone
in his hand for twenty minutes.

2
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:08,744
Nine times he'd tried to call.

3
00:00:08,784 --> 00:00:12,736
Nine times he'd stopped
just short of the button.

4
00:00:12,776 --> 00:00:17,503
Six days into the war, he hadn't
called his parents once —

5
00:00:17,543 --> 00:00:22,187
afraid that his mother's voice
would make all of it real.

6
00:00:22,227 --> 00:00:23,653
He finally dialed.

7
00:00:23,693 --> 00:00:28,297
She picked up on the second
ring, past midnight in Seoul.

8
00:00:28,337 --> 00:00:29,845
She'd been waiting.

9
00:00:29,885 --> 00:00:30,496
“Junho.”

10
00:00:30,536 --> 00:00:32,615
Two syllables were enough.

11
00:00:32,655 --> 00:00:37,503
“I'm alive,” he said, his voice
steadier than he'd expected.

12
00:00:37,543 --> 00:00:39,051
“I know,” she said.

13
00:00:39,091 --> 00:00:42,961
“We've been watching the
news. Your father too.”

14
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:48,990
A short silence, then her voice dropped
to almost a whisper. “Sleep well.”

15
00:00:49,030 --> 00:00:55,426
She asked nothing else — not when he'd
come home, not whether it was dangerous.

16
00:00:55,466 --> 00:01:01,169
Not asking was how she said: I already
know everything, and I'll wait.
